[node name="Route" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "WHAT PROGRESS IS: the arc swept so far on the one lap, taken at the lane radius. IT IS DATA, AND IT LIVES ON THE MAP. The deck height, radial band, lane radius, entry angle and exit angle are here, and MatchLapTracker, RingRunner, the HUD and the round card all read them from here rather than from a second copy."
script = ExtResource("5_ring_route")

[node name="Level1" type="Node3D" parent="Route"]
editor_description = "Level 1: deck y=23.0, r44.0-r60.0, lane r=52.0, 5 deg to 335 deg = 330 deg of lap, 299 m. Its exit is the finish of the whole route."
script = ExtResource("6_ring_level")
deck_height = 23.0000
inner_radius = 46.7000
outer_radius = 57.3000
lane_radius = 52.0000
entry_angle_degrees = 5.0000
exit_angle_degrees = 335.0000
ramp_foot_radius = 0.0000
ramp_landing_radius = 0.0000

[node name="Tower" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The tower, and its origin is the FLOOR OF THE GUARD ROOM at y=25.35. That is the model's own datum: assets/models/tower.glb hangs its rock 36.4 m below this point and carries the top of its drum 9.6 m above it, so the model drops in at identity and TowerSpawn, the lights and the Watcher all hang off the same floor.\n\nTHE GUARD IS INSIDE IT NOW. A hollow chamber 10.2 m across with eight openings.\n\nTHE DECK IS AT THE GUARD'S EYE. Ryan: \"raise the top one to eye level.\" The eye is this floor plus 1.65 m = y=27.00, and the deck's walking surface is exactly there, so the guard looks flat along the whole ring."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0, 0, 1, 0, 25.35, 0)

[node name="Rock" parent="Tower" instance=ExtResource("8_tower_model")]
editor_description = "assets/models/tower.glb: the column, the drum and the hollow chamber, one mesh. It carries its OWN collision (a -colonly shape in the glTF), so the guard stands on the model's floor and is stopped by the model's stone -- there is no second, invisible copy of either in this scene, and nothing here can drift out of agreement with what you can see.\n\nIts origin is the floor of the guard room, which is why it drops in at identity: see the Tower node above."

[node name="TowerSpawn" type="Marker3D" parent="Tower"]
editor_description = "On the chamber floor, 0.25 m up. The clearance is deliberate: spawning a capsule with its feet exactly on the collision plane overlaps it, and depenetration launches the body across the arena. The model's origin IS this floor, so this is origin + 0.25 and nothing else."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0, 0, 1, 0, 0.25, 0)

[node name="KeyLight" type="DirectionalLight3D" parent="Tower"]
editor_description = "Fire from the hole above, angled 20 degrees off vertical (about 70 deg below horizontal) into the pit rather than the flat noon light of an office."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.34202, 0.939693, 0, -0.939693, 0.34202, 0, 20, 0)
light_color = Color(1.0, 0.45, 0.15, 1.0)
light_energy = 0.0
shadow_enabled = false
shadow_bias = 0.08
shadow_normal_bias = 2.0
directional_shadow_mode = 0
directional_shadow_max_distance = 180.

[node name="HellFlood" type="OmniLight3D" parent="Tower"]
light_color = Color(1.0, 0.28, 0.06, 1)
light_energy = 3.4
shadow_enabled = false
omni_range = 700.0
omni_attenuation = 0.6
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 300, 0)

[node name="TowerLight" type="OmniLight3D" parent="Tower"]
editor_description = "LOCAL GLOW ONLY, not the arena's main light -- see KeyLight. A small hot point above the platform so the tower still visibly reads as a light source up close. Colour, energy, range, attenuation and height are TowerLightProfile fields applied by TowerLight.gd at ready; the light_* properties here are placeholders for the editor view. It rides the tower's rise, which is the point."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0, 0, 1, 0, 10, 0)
light_color = Color(0.9, 0.14, 0.08, 1.0)
light_energy = 30.0
omni_range = 25.0
omni_attenuation = 1.0
shadow_enabled = true
omni_shadow_mode = 1
script = ExtResource("3_tower_light")
profile = ExtResource("4_tower_light_profile")

[node name="Watcher" parent="Tower" instance=ExtResource("7_watching_eye")]
editor_description = "THE EYE THAT FOLLOWS YOU. assets/models/eye.glb -- a 5 m ball with a glowing iris -- hanging over the guard's stand and turned so its pupil points at whoever is looking at it. Ryan played it and kept it.\n\nHEIGHT: WatchingEyeProfile.height_metres is 7.2, and it did not need retuning. The node places itself at (0, height, 0) in THIS NODE'S space, and the tower's local frame is exactly what it was -- the whole rise is the Tower transform. So the ball still floats 7.2 m above the platform surface: world y=39.35, spanning y=36.85 to y=41.85, which is 1.9 m clear of the guard's crown below it and far under KeyLight above it. It is the only thing in the tower's space between the guard and the light now that the box of eyes is gone, and at that height it is in clear sky from the deck.\n\nIT LEAKS NOTHING. It orients toward the local Viewport's own camera, so on every client it resolves to that client's player and every prisoner sees the pupil on themselves. The orientation is a pure function of the POSITION of the local camera -- not its direction, not the guard, not the seat, not the rifle -- so it carries zero bits about anybody except the person reading it. A camera inside the tower's own column is not watched at all.\n\nNOT EDITED HERE. scenes/tower/ and scripts/tower/ belong to the eye; this scene owns the instance and its parent, and nothing else."
profile = ExtResource("9_watcher_profile")
